# What the image build is allowed to see.
#
# This is an allowlist -- everything is excluded, then the few paths the build
# genuinely needs are added back -- rather than a copy of .gitignore. Docker
# does not read .gitignore, so a denylist here would ship whatever the next
# ticket adds to the repository root. The specific thing an allowlist prevents
# is `var/darts.db`: a real database with real matches in it, sitting in the
# build context of an image that gets copied to a Pi.
#
# It also keeps the context small. Denying nothing sends ~353 MB (.venv is a
# macOS-arm64 virtualenv that is useless to a linux image, frontend/node_modules
# is reinstalled by `npm ci` in the build anyway); this allowlist sends ~2 MB.
*

# The Python stage: dependency resolution, then the package itself.
# README.md and LICENSE are here because pyproject.toml's `readme` and
# `license` point at them, so hatchling cannot build the wheel without them.
!pyproject.toml
!uv.lock
!README.md
!LICENSE
!backend

# The Node stage. `npm run build` is `tsc -b && vite build`, and tsconfig.json
# references the test project as well as the app, so type-checking needs the
# whole source tree -- tests included -- not just what Vite bundles.
!frontend

# The entrypoint, which the runtime stage COPYs in.
!deploy

# Re-excluded from the directories added back above. node_modules is what
# `npm ci` rebuilds from package-lock.json inside the image, and copying a
# macOS one in would defeat the point of installing at all.
frontend/node_modules
frontend/dist
frontend/coverage
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
